WI-kuliv. `coverage-select select` answers the same question `shadow`
does, but BEFORE pytest rather than after, and smart-test unions the
answer into the local run set.

BELOW THE SEAM, which is the point of cutting the seam last week. The
committed manifest drives the merge-gating CI (woodpecker.yml:380), so
landing the union above the capture would have added roughly 44 test
files per informative run to what CI runs -- a slower gate AND a slower
local run, invisible in any test. Verified rather than argued: the
manifest this script writes is byte-identical to the one the pre-Phase-2
script writes over the same tree, timestamp excluded.

ADDITIVE, NEVER SUBTRACTIVE. That is the property the phase rests on and
why it precedes narrowing (Phase 3, WI-bolot): a union cannot drop a
test, so the worst case is wasted time. The justification is not speed --
this makes local runs slower -- it is that coverage sees runtime
dependencies the static import graph cannot. Measured on this tree: a
change to edge_types.find_edge_type selects test_cli_explain.py, which
imports nothing the slice could follow, because `explain` looks edge
types up at runtime.

SELECTIONS ARE FILTERED AGAINST THE FILESYSTEM. The index is persistent
and out-of-repo, nothing prunes it on a rename, and pytest treats a
missing path as a collection ERROR rather than a skip. An unfiltered
union would fail runs it was only meant to widen, which is the opposite
of "can only add tests".

THE SHADOW NOW GRADES AGAINST THE PRE-UNION SET, found by reading a live
run rather than by reasoning. With the union wired, the shadow reported
EXTRA_FROM_COVERAGE: 0 -- unfalsifiable, because the union had already
folded coverage's picks into the set the shadow compares against. That
metric is what WI-kuliv is justified BY (7 of the first 10 observations
added a test), so the phase would have destroyed its own measurement and
the flatline would have read as "coverage stopped finding anything".
MANIFEST_TESTS is the pre-union set, and it is what the first 10
observations were compared against, so the series stays continuous.

Guards EXECUTE the shipped shell block against a stub selector rather
than pattern-matching it: a union that quietly adds nothing satisfies
every position check ever written, and on the day this landed a live run
legitimately added zero because the slice already had all 3 picks. The
off-switch case runs the same stub and asserts the opposite outcome, so
the ADD path is shown to fire rather than assumed to.

